f 1053 #uuid "64f2826e-10ec-5427-8fd0-5dacd740fef4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097413 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097414 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097413 #edb/ref 1061 12306 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097413 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9f76f2b2-574f-5f45-a54b-c55d5040cccd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097413 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186097813 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097414 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097415 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097414 #edb/ref 1061 12307 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097414 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "49950076-5f24-57dd-96a0-b8b061b4f2cb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097414 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096610 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097415 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097416 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097415 #edb/ref 1061 12308 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097415 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ef920bbd-db8e-5c63-82fa-370c8e9f05e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097415 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096611 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097416 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097417 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097416 #edb/ref 1061 12309 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097416 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ef1a628c-101c-57a3-a8d3-5ce0731832a5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097416 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186097814 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097417 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097418 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097417 #edb/ref 1061 12310 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097417 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d2eb3d3f-2d57-59c0-b5a0-4253946c9cf7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097417 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096612 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097418 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097749 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097418 #edb/ref 1061 12311 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097418 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "be9c264f-1e13-55c5-83f7-3217ce14b437" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097418 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186097815 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097749 #edb/ref 1061 461037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097749 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "91e627df-d8f4-581a-bf44-76bf1bb88674" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097749 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186097806 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097806 #edb/ref 1064 "Now, let's derive the rule\n![](images/77/77334bed6aafc3383552d90bcfc8da614d56493edce4e7ab89a2f28e01d3dbfa.svg)\n\nThe trick here is to write this in terms of ![](images/5b/5ba79af546498192229d0cdd5a4a922d1d015802402b8eec5910fe00f999820d.svg) \n\nFirst, note that since the natural logarithm is the inverse of the exponential function, we have\n![](images/09/091c69568c8472aacf8229a756a835e0edc26700677e4fa67de3d2f6ac0d96a2.svg)\n\nand by the power rule for logarithms, we can write this as\n\n![](images/c9/c9b146d550ef068823a4ee4b9f63eea89f46d6ceecedf0ad4baa6462f11d9127.svg)\n\nNow, the following result can be used (we'll prove it in the subsequent topics):\n\n![](images/ce/cedfc7ab127ac8b34cd72b21e8c3e527541e054721324d9d948d6df123cd61e0.svg)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n![](images/58/5880fb665abda7f3cef4ad7425c99c43b16e84c448c7b9e22ff32f76e36df87c.svg)\n\nas required." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097806 #edb/ref 1065 13257 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097806 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "551a7005-80c0-5cee-b28e-f3b565aaf250" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097806 #edb/ref 1067 "Justifying the Second Rule" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097813 #edb/ref 1064 "The exponential function  $f(x) = e^x$ has the special property that its derivative is the function itself:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{ \\textrm{d} x}\\left( e^x \\right)= e^x\n$$\n\nSo, taking the derivative of an exponential function does nothing to the exponential function. The exponential function remains exactly the same. \n\nNote that the exponential function is the *only* function with this special property.\n\nWe'll justify this result at the end of the lesson. But for now, let's get some practice working with it." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097813 #edb/ref 1065 2611 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097813 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "a71b1a8d-93f4-5e48-ab3a-bd7220d50f18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097813 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097814 #edb/ref 1064 "If we replace  the base $e$ of an exponential function by any other positive number $a$, then the derivative is as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{ \\textrm{d} x}\\left( a^x \\right)= a^x \\ln a\n$$\n\nWe just multiply the given exponential function by the natural logarithm of the base.\n\nNote that since $\\ln e =1$, our first formula is a particular case of this one!\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{ \\textrm{d} x}\\left( e^x \\right)= e^x \\ln e = e^x \\cdot 1 = e^x\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097814 #edb/ref 1065 2612 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097814 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "061a5c54-700a-5793-b266-cf156584544a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097814 #edb/ref 1067 "Differentiating an Exponential Function with a Base Other Than e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097815 #edb/ref 1064 "To derive the identity\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(e^x) = e^x,\n$$\n\nwe begin with the definition of the derivative:\n\nwhere $f(x) = e^x$.\n\nSubstituting the function $f(x)$ into the definition of $f'(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={lim}_{h\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{x+h}-{e}^{x}}{h} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{h}-{e}^{x}}{h} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{x}\\cdot ({e}^{h}-1)}{h} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\cdot {lim}_{h\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{h}-1}{h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, it can be shown that\n\n$$\n\\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{e^h - 1}{h} = 1,\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\nf'(x) = e^x \\cdot 1 = e^x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(e^x) = e^x.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097815 #edb/ref 1065 2613 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097815 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "1b006e01-04f6-5f6b-b435-b0f89163d7a1" #edb/ref 175921860454