t $f(x)={6}^{x}+5{e}^{x}$, find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479960 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "50148e2c-17f0-5238-804f-16d18ed920ad" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479960 #edb/ref 1074 "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({6}^{x}+5{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({6}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({6}^{x})+5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}) \\\\  & ={6}^{x}\\ln 6+5{e}^{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & ={({6}^{x}\\ln 6+5{e}^{x})|}_{x=0} \\\\  & ={6}^{0}\\ln 6+5{e}^{0} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\ln 6+5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\ln 6+5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479963 #edb/ref 1080 "\\ln 6" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479963 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479963 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "556ea93d-c41f-51e1-a3d5-3a153a74e606" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479964 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186479992 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479964 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479964 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $f(x) = 5 \\cdot 6^{x}$, find $f^{′}(x)$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479964 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "582239d0-9d5e-5fbf-8b8c-312d6a4b25f3" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479964 #edb/ref 1074 "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{′}(x)&=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5 \\cdot 6^{x}) \\\\ &=5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6^{x}) \\\\ &=5\\cdot 6^{x}\\ln 6 \\\\ &=5\\ln 6\\cdot 6^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479971 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186479978 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479971 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479971 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $f(x) = 9^{x} + 1e^{x}$, find $f^{′}(x)$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479971 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "90f05299-4aec-5aef-a19d-5af09d844fc9" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479971 #edb/ref 1074 "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{′}(x)&=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9^{x}+1e^{x}) \\\\ &=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1e^{x}) \\\\ &=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9^{x})+1\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(e^{x}) \\\\ &=9^{x}\\ln 9+1e^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479973 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186479942 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479973 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479973 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $f(x)=6\\cdot {8}^{x}+4x+1$, find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479973 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9227db0a-2b43-5781-8e85-e3ce3701dc2c" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479973 #edb/ref 1074 "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6\\cdot {8}^{x}+4x+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6\\cdot {8}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\  & =6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({8}^{x})+4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\  & =6(\\ln (8){8}^{x})+4(1)+0 \\\\  & =6\\ln (8){8}^{x}+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479974 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186479940 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479974 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479974 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $f(x)={3}^{x}-9{x}^{2}+5x-8$, find ${f}^{′}(x).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479974 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9b5eb51d-f8f2-5555-81b1-c63476f8f13a" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479974 #edb/ref 1074 "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({3}^{x}-9{x}^{2}+5x-8) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({3}^{x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9{x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({3}^{x})-9\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8) \\\\  & =\\ln 3\\cdot {3}^{x}-9(2x)+5(1)-0 \\\\  & ={3}^{x}\\ln 3-18x+5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479976 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186479953 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479976 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479976 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $f(x)={3}^{x}+9{e}^{x}$, find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479976 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9f8d11c7-1ce6-57ae-a750-00abfd861493" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479976 #edb/ref 1074 "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({3}^{x}+9{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({3}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({3}^{x})+9\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}) \\\\  & ={3}^{x}\\ln 3+9{e}^{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & ={({3}^{x}\\ln 3+9{e}^{x})|}_{x=0} \\\\  & ={3}^{0}\\ln 3+9{e}^{0} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\ln 3+9\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\ln 3+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479981 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186479952 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479981 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479981 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $f(x)=2\\cdot {2}^{x}+3\\cdot {4}^{x}-4x^2+5$, find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1.$\n\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479981 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b4aa7414-d170-5940-95df-f23e78929052" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479981 #edb/ref 1074 "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\cdot {2}^{x}+3\\cdot {4}^{x}-4x^2+5) \\\\ &=2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({2}^{x})+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({4}^{x})-4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x^2)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5) \\\\ &=2({2}^{x}\\ln(2))+3({4}^{x}\\ln(4))-4(2x)+0 \\\\ &=2\\ln(2)\\cdot {2}^{x}+3\\ln(4)\\cdot {4}^{x}-8x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(1)&=2\\ln(2)\\cdot {2}^{(1)}+3\\ln(4)\\cdot {4}^{(1)}-8(1) \\\\ &=2(2)\\ln(2)+3(4)\\ln(4)-(8)(1) \\\\ &=-8 + 4 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 12 \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479982 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186479965 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479982 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479982 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $f(x)=2\\cdot {4}^{x}+1\\cdot {5}^{x}-3x^2+4$, find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1.$\n\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479982 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b995540b-f7ab-55d7-8f91-c51d207d2180" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479982 #edb/ref 1074 "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\cdot {4}^{x}+1\\cdot {5}^{x}-3x^2+4) \\\\ &=2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({4}^{x})+1\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({5}^{x})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x^2)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4) \\\\ &=2({4}^{x}\\ln(4))+1({5}^{x}\\ln(5))-3(2x)+0 \\\\ &=2\\ln(4)\\cdot {4}^{x}+1\\ln(5)\\cdot {5}^{x}-6x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(1)&=2\\ln(4)\\cdot {4}^{(1)}+1\\ln(5)\\cdot {5}^{(1)}-6(1) \\\\ &=2(4)\\ln(4)+1(5)\\ln(5)-(6)(1) \\\\ &=-6 + 5 \\ln{\\left(5 \\right)} + 8 \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479984 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186479944 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479984 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479984 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479984 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186479944 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479984 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c6f7efb5-5352-5998-97f1-7e7dd561f8f9" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479985 #edb/ref 1080 "6" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479985 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479985 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c713293d-b983-5584-b151-359e1e3a8af8" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479989 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186479984 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479989 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479989 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $f(x)=1\\cdot {5}^{x}+2\\cdot {2}^{x}-3x^2+1$, find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=-1.$\n\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479989 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cf41a068-fd0d-5f4b-9f3b-52ecb794226b" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479989 #edb/ref 1074 "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1\\cdot {5}^{x}+2\\cdot {2}^{x}-3x^2+1) \\\\ &=1\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({5}^{x})+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({2}^{x})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x^2)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ &=1({5}^{x}\\ln(5))+2({2}^{x}\\ln(2))-3(2x)+0 \\\\ &=1\\ln(5)\\cdot {5}^{x}+2\\ln(2)\\cdot {2}^{x}-6x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(-1)&=1\\ln(5)\\cdot {5}^{(-1)}+2\\ln(2)\\cdot {2}^{(-1)}-6(-1) \\\\ &=1(\\frac{1}{5})\\ln(5)+2(\\frac{1}{2})\\ln(2)-(6)(-1) \\\\ &=\\frac{\\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}}{5} + \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479990 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186479987 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479990 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479990 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $f(x)={7}^{x}-7{x}^{3}+4x-1$, the slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479990 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "df5079ea-2748-53c3-9b3e-39ecdb2bea5f" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479990 #edb/ref 1074 "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({7}^{x}-7{x}^{3}+4x-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({7}^{x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7{x}^{3})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({7}^{x})-7\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})+4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\  & =\\ln (7)\\cdot {7}^{x}-7(3{x}^{2})+4(1)-0 \\\\  & =\\ln (7)\\cdot {7}^{x}-21{x}^{2}+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & ={(\\ln (7)\\cdot {7}^{x}-21{x}^{2}+4)|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =\\ln (7)\\cdot {7}^{0}-21(0)^{2}+4 \\\\  & =\\ln (7)\\cdot 1-0+4 \\\\  & =\\ln (7)+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479991 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186479948 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479991 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479991 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479991 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186479948 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479991 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e1395a30-edad-54d2-9382-c62a8875aa3f" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479993 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186479991 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479993 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479993 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $f(x)={9}^{x}-1{x}^{3}+2x-1$, the slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479993 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ec00e600-a612-5a76-94ca-79ecaa3d171e" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479993 #edb/ref 1074 "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({9}^{x}-1{x}^{3}+2x-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({9}^{x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1{x}^{3})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({9}^{x})-1\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6) \\\\  & =\\ln (9)\\cdot {9}^{x}-1(3{x}^{2})+2(1)-0 \\\\  & =\\ln (9)\\cdot {9}^{x}-3{x}^{2}+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & ={(\\ln (9)\\cdot {9}^{x}-3{x}^{2}+2)|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =\\ln (9)\\cdot {9}^{0}-3(0)^{2}+2 \\\\  & =\\ln (9)\\cdot 1-0+2 \\\\  & =\\ln (9)+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479996 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186479970 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479996 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479996 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $f(x)=2\\cdot {6}^{x}+1\\cdot {3}^{x}-3x^2+2$, find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=-1.$\n\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479996 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f8120d99-4d4d-56ef-af5e-c92f6fe86369" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479996 #edb/ref 1074 "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\cdot {6}^{x}+1\\cdot {3}^{x}-3x^2+2) \\\\ &=2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({6}^{x})+1\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({3}^{x})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x^2)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2) \\\\ &=2({6}^{x}\\ln(6))+1({3}^{x}\\ln(3))-3(2x)+0 \\\\ &=2\\ln(6)\\cdot {6}^{x}+1\\ln(3)\\cdot {3}^{x}-6x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(-1)&=2\\ln(6)\\cdot {6}^{(-1)}+1\\ln(3)\\cdot {3}^{(-1)}-6(-1) \\\\ &=2(\\frac{1}{6})\\ln(6)+1(\\frac{1}{3})\\ln(3)-(6)(-1) \\\\ &=\\frac{\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}{3} + \\frac{\\ln{\\left(6 \\right)}}{3} + 6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479997 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186096612.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479997 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "1a5c3131-e07d-52bf-8fa5-e96ba318a4bc" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479998 #edb/ref 